---
import Terminal from '../layouts/Terminal.astro';
---

<Terminal title="about">
	<p class="cmd">man infrashift</p>

	<article class="man">
		<header class="man-head dim">
			<span>INFRASHIFT(7)</span>
			<span>Organization Manual</span>
			<span>INFRASHIFT(7)</span>
		</header>

		<h2>NAME</h2>
		<p>infrashift - trusted infrastructure, built in the open</p>

		<h2>SYNOPSIS</h2>
		<p><b>infrashift</b> [<i>--signed</i>] [<i>--reproducible</i>] [<i>--tui</i>]</p>

		<h2>DESCRIPTION</h2>
		<p>
			infrashift builds the unglamorous foundations that platform teams depend on: base images,
			development environments, policy, and automation.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our focus is software supply chain security. Artifacts are signed, ship with SBOMs and
			provenance, and build reproducibly, so you can verify exactly what you run and where it came
			from. Security and compliance are shifted left into the tools engineers already use, rather
			than bolted on at the end.
		</p>
		<p>
			We choose fast, keyboard-driven TUIs over bloated, slow web UIs. Our tools live in the
			terminal where engineers already work, which keeps context switching to a minimum.
		</p>

		<h2>SEE ALSO</h2>
		<p><a href="/projects/">projects</a>(1), <a href="/contact/">contact</a>(1)</p>
	</article>
</Terminal>

<style>
	.man-head {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1ch;
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0.25rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		color: var(--magenta);
	}

	.man p {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem 4ch;
		color: var(--fg-dim);
	}

	b {
		color: var(--fg);
	}

	i {
		font-style: normal;
		color: var(--yellow);
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.man-head span:nth-child(2) {
			display: none;
		}

		.man p {
			margin-left: 2ch;
		}
	}
</style>
